class.description:
[VideoTextureSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"video_texture"[/code]: it stores the texture filtering ([member Viewport.anisotropic_filtering_level], [member Viewport.texture_mipmap_bias], [method RenderingServer.light_projectors_set_filter], [method RenderingServer.decals_set_filter]) and the Canvas2D options ([member Viewport.canvas_item_default_texture_filter], [member Viewport.canvas_item_default_texture_repeat], [member Viewport.snap_2d_transforms_to_pixel], [member Viewport.snap_2d_vertices_to_pixel], [member Viewport.sdf_oversize], [member Viewport.sdf_scale], [method RenderingServer.canvas_set_shadow_texture_size]) for the player. Every value takes effect at once. The settings resource is a [VideoTextureSettings]; the file is [code]user://settings/video_texture.ini[/code] by default, in the format of [member ProjectSettings.settings/storage/format].
When the game starts, the stored values are applied in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SCENE], after the root viewport exists and before the main scene is loaded. Values set earlier wait until then. The defaults are the project settings ([member ProjectSettings.rendering/textures/default_filters/anisotropic_filtering_level], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/textures/default_filters/texture_mipmap_bias], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/textures/light_projectors/filter], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/textures/decals/filter], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/textures/canvas_textures/default_texture_filter], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/textures/canvas_textures/default_texture_repeat], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/2d/snap/snap_2d_transforms_to_pixel], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/2d/snap/snap_2d_vertices_to_pixel], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/2d/sdf/oversize], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/2d/sdf/scale], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/2d/shadow_atlas/size]), with their feature overrides such as [code].mobile[/code].
[b]Further viewports:[/b] the per-viewport values also go to the viewports added with [method add_viewport] and to every [Viewport] in the group [method get_viewport_group], for example a [SubViewport] that renders a pixel-art game at a low resolution.
[b]Renderers:[/b] every value works in every renderer, except the light projector filter and the decal filter, which the Compatibility renderer (default in the Web export) ignores. [method SettingsServer.is_value_supported] returns [code]false[/code] for them there and [method get_unsupported_setting_names] lists them, so that a settings menu can gray them out. Such values are still stored, but not pushed; a warning names them once.
Values out of range are clamped with a warning: [code]texture_mipmap_bias[/code] [code]-2.0[/code] to [code]2.0[/code], [code]canvas_shadow_atlas_size[/code] [code]128[/code] to [code]16384[/code]. An enum value out of range is replaced by the default.
Texture streaming has its own domain, [VideoTextureStreamingSettingsServer], which exists only when the engine is built with the [code]texture_streaming[/code] module.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	$Anisotropy.selected = VideoTextureSettingsServer.get_anisotropic_filtering_level()
	$PixelSnap.button_pressed = VideoTextureSettingsServer.is_snap_2d_transforms_to_pixel_enabled()
	$DecalFilter.disabled = not VideoTextureSettingsServer.is_value_supported(&"decal_filter")

func _on_anisotropy_item_selected(index):
	VideoTextureSettingsServer.set_anisotropic_filtering_level(index as Viewport.AnisotropicFiltering)

func _on_pixel_snap_toggled(toggled_on):
	VideoTextureSettingsServer.set_snap_2d_transforms_to_pixel(toggled_on)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    GetNode<OptionButton>("Anisotropy").Selected = (int)VideoTextureSettingsServer.GetAnisotropicFilteringLevel();
    GetNode<CheckBox>("PixelSnap").ButtonPressed = VideoTextureSettingsServer.IsSnap2DTransformsToPixelEnabled();
    // Methods of the base class are called through Singleton.
    GetNode<OptionButton>("DecalFilter").Disabled = !VideoTextureSettingsServer.Singleton.IsValueSupported("decal_filter");
}

private void OnAnisotropyItemSelected(long index)
{
    VideoTextureSettingsServer.SetAnisotropicFilteringLevel((Viewport.AnisotropicFiltering)index);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] In C#, the static class [code skip-lint]VideoTextureSettingsServer[/code] only has the methods of this class. The methods of [SettingsServer] are called through [code]VideoTextureSettingsServer.Singleton[/code].
[b]Note:[/b] A game that sets these properties on the root viewport itself overwrites the player's values until they are applied again. The domain is never applied to the editor itself.
